# Line endings are a correctness concern in this repo, not a style preference.
#
# `domain/text.py` canonicalizes to LF + NFC on ingest and stores the canonical form,
# so a stored hash is always verifiable against the stored text (plan/stage-0-decisions.md
# §1). The tests that pin that behaviour compare canonicalized output against string
# literals living in these source files. If `core.autocrlf=true` — which is set globally
# on the machine this repo was first committed from — rewrote those literals to CRLF on
# checkout, the line-ending tests would be asserting against the very thing they exist to
# normalize away, and would pass or fail depending on the platform.
#
# litharness-contracts solves the same hazard the other way (`* -text`, no conversion at
# all) because it stores golden fixtures verified by SHA-256 over exact byte ranges. Here
# the working tree, not the object store, is what has to be predictable, so normalize to
# LF on both sides.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish artifacts that must never be translated.
*.db binary
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
